Origin uncertain. Several origins have been proposed for the Norwegian name:
# a dialectal spelling variant of Gjul, related to Gjurd and Gyrd, perhaps ultimately from Old Norse Guðfrøðr m, a dithematic name whose elements mean “god” and “peace”;
# a short form of Julius;
# Old Danish Jul m, a younger form of Old Norse Ígull m, from ígull (“hedgehog; sea urchin”).
Compare Danish Jul and Swedish Jul (“male given name”).
